      },
      "lineNbr": 171,
      "author": {
        "id": 1221725
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-12-17T22:01:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Shouldn\u0027t need to re-initialize any data structures, since the only place the IOException could happen is as part of the readFromDisk() call. I\u0027ve moved the code to make that more obvious.\n\nAdded an immediate retry; I\u0027d prefer to not add the complexity of retrying after a delay, and it should handle most transients (disk read failure, etc).",
      "parentUuid": "16bc6719_80bd235b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 171,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 171,
        "endChar": 69
      },
      "revId": "4a723b3ee3dc9d76ec8eeadd906e395daf5cfe06",
