      },
      "lineNbr": 225,
      "author": {
        "id": 1060151
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-12-16T01:30:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "At first glance, it looks to me like we should be blocking systemReady() on the initial load from disk of the configs. No?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 225,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 225,
        "endChar": 57
      },
      "revId": "4a723b3ee3dc9d76ec8eeadd906e395daf5cfe06",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "557432f0_175a23ac",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/VcnManagementService.java",
        "patchSetId": 15
      },
      "lineNbr": 225,
      "author": {
        "id": 1221725
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-12-17T22:01:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Not particularly necessary. I\u0027m trying to avoid making changes that may significantly affect system boot time, to minimize impact on system health. In the worst case, we\u0027ll trigger the VCN startup after underlying networks come up, but that\u0027s trivial with a mutable capability.\n\nProbably a legacy of a rebase, but this is already addressed in the startup-read in the constructor.",
      "parentUuid": "7a3e3ab0_cf2cd94a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 225,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 225,
        "endChar": 57
      },
      "revId": "4a723b3ee3dc9d76ec8eeadd906e395daf5cfe06",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c141dc9d_69870d47",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/VcnManagementService.java",
        "patchSetId": 15
      },
      "lineNbr": 225,
      "author": {
        "id": 1060151
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-12-18T00:34:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I didn\u0027t realize this would impact system health. I was just thinking that we need to be sure that the read from disk happens before the pull from keystore (not implemented) and the network provider registration, no? But since the disk load isn\u0027t on the thread that\u0027s initializing services... not likely to block is it?\n\nOr, alternatively, should systemReady register the provider on the HandlerThread?",
      "parentUuid": "557432f0_175a23ac",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 225,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 225,
        "endChar": 57
      },
      "revId": "4a723b3ee3dc9d76ec8eeadd906e395daf5cfe06",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
